                            {
                                "target_word": "lament",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97da2a4f-74cd-3625-acbe-f88d34c8e773",
                                        "entry_id": "c9fbf2ff-3ba7-30a6-9379-531ea8d82c1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To express grief; to weep or wail; to mourn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cf65efb-1b61-44a9-85f3-9919382ab3b2",
                                                "sense_id": "97da2a4f-74cd-3625-acbe-f88d34c8e773",
                                                "text": "Ye shall weep and lament, but the world shall rejoice."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0320b4f2-e1ad-3837-8093-7f73d67f83ba",
                                        "entry_id": "c9fbf2ff-3ba7-30a6-9379-531ea8d82c1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To express great sorrow or regret over; to bewail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94be9d4f-b1ce-460c-a7ce-8d0296b58dba",
                                                "sense_id": "0320b4f2-e1ad-3837-8093-7f73d67f83ba",
                                                "text": "Euston is so traditionally a part of the London scene that many will lament the passing of the old station when rebuilding is complete in readiness for the new electric service, which will probably be by multiple-units between Euston and Wolverhampton."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b54b535-ea1d-4d25-8285-eddef2c4030a",
                                                "sense_id": "0320b4f2-e1ad-3837-8093-7f73d67f83ba",
                                                "text": "By the end, Sunderland were lucky to lose by the same scoreline Northampton Town suffered against Southampton, in 1921. The Sunderland manager, Gus Poyet, lamented that it was “the most embarrassed I’ve ever been on a football pitch, without a doubt”."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3b19626-4e56-4a69-bef6-deb19191f1ca",
                                                "sense_id": "0320b4f2-e1ad-3837-8093-7f73d67f83ba",
                                                "text": "One laugh'd at follies, one lamented crimes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6ccdb5c-ba3c-4d4f-ad43-2299df1d8e74",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6dad4b5-370e-3766-b078-7b766434515d",
                        "source_sense_id": "2edf8716-821d-3d4c-baed-56aeb89bdc25",
                        "target_lang_word": "dirge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dirge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25f32099-7830-39c2-8ca2-d16edba5a847",
                                        "entry_id": "5944064b-d674-322d-868b-c0737860ccce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mournful poem or piece of music composed or performed as a memorial to a dead person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d059ecf-793d-485a-b13b-ab0113aa6f74",
                                                "sense_id": "25f32099-7830-39c2-8ca2-d16edba5a847",
                                                "text": "Therefore our ſometimes Siſter, now our Queen, / Th’ imperiall Ioyntreſſe of this warlike State, / Haue we, as ’twere, with a defeated ioy, / With one Auſpicious, and one Dropping eye, / With mirth in Funerall, and with Dirge in Marriage, / In equall Scale weighing Delight and Dole / Taken to Wife […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c769213-cbf4-4b18-b1c3-9396c460f2d2",
                                                "sense_id": "25f32099-7830-39c2-8ca2-d16edba5a847",
                                                "text": "While I watched the tempest, so beautiful yet terrific, I wandered on with a hasty step. This noble war in the sky elevated my spirits; I clasped my hands, and exclaimed aloud, “William, dear angel! this is thy funeral, this thy dirge!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71a1a3ae-cf6f-4703-9e3c-5640aa92b317",
                                                "sense_id": "25f32099-7830-39c2-8ca2-d16edba5a847",
                                                "text": "It was as if the night sang dirges with clenched teeth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "160cf3cb-c2f9-497b-802d-e91fd265da94",
                                                "sense_id": "25f32099-7830-39c2-8ca2-d16edba5a847",
                                                "text": "Over six sections – a prologue, a life-story, a dream-quest, a dirge, a masque and an epilogue – they meditate on their lives, their hopes, their losses, and on the human condition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ba40955-9ff7-3429-913a-43c2d6ead04d",
                                        "entry_id": "5944064b-d674-322d-868b-c0737860ccce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A song or piece of music that is considered too slow, bland or boring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
